  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Refining and Assisting Digital Health Transformation Strategy (DHTS 2025-2029) Implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project with AMANA aims to provide technical assistance in advancing the Digital Health Transformation Strategy (DHTS) 2025&#x2013;2029, by translating the strategic document into a tangible and measurable five-year implementation roadmap. This roadmap will serve as a practical guide to ensure the effective execution of the strategy. 

The overarching goal of the project is to support the successful implementation of digital health transformation in Indonesia by enhancing stakeholder readiness through three key activities: 
- Refinement of the Digital Health Transformation Strategy (2025&#x2013;2029) 
- Development of the DHTS Implementation Roadmap 
- Stakeholder Capacity Building and Technical Support for Roadmap Implementation 

The Digital Health Transformation Strategy (DHTS) 2025&#x2013;2029 and its accompanying roadmap are not standalone documents. They serve as strategic policy instruments aligned with broader national development goals. Specifically, they support the Ministry of Health&#x2019;s agenda as outlined in the Health Sector Master Plan (Rencana Induk Bidang Kesehatan [RIBK]) 2025&#x2013;2029, the National Medium-Term Development Plan (Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Menengah Nasional [RPJMN]) 2025&#x2013;2029, and ultimately contribute to the National Long-Term Development Plan (Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Panjang [RPJP]) 2025&#x2013;2045.</narrative>
  </description>
